comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-25T06:39:21.754Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation: pm package list, pm packages list and pm extension list are now aliases of pm package inventory (Commander alias moved off catalog; alias contracts owner pm-gh1777, extension list targets package inventory because the deprecated extension vocabulary has no live-contract inventory row); catalog keeps the bundled catalog. Inventory rows gain update (last observed newer version for the installed version) and the result gains updates_available. One --fields contract (parseListingFields/projectListingRows, published with the inventory reader so the CLI stays on the SDK export closure) on list, explore, manage and catalog; unknown keys are refused as 'must be one of a|b|c', which recovery turns into allowed_values. Default explore/manage rows drop the embedded contributions map (--fields ...,contributions restores it). pm extensions list now suggests package list with an executable --help retry: a singular/plural slip of a noun that is neither a command nor an alias resolves through the alias contracts, then follows typed operands. Measured on this repo: package list 574 B (was 11,976 B, the catalog); explore 5,991 to 3,837 B; manage 6,018 to 3,864 B. Static fast path covers list. Gates: grammar, flag contracts, contracts fixture, completion, SDK surface (two additive inventory type changes acknowledged), static chain green."
  "2026-11-25T08:10:09.507Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 1 fixes on the listing side: pm package --global list (scope switch before the verb) now stays on the static no-activation path (Codex P1); explore/manage validate --fields at action admission, before adoption, remote checks or observation writes (Codex P2); pm extension explore/manage --fields keep their subcommand route instead of the legacy root rewrite (Codex P2); catalog --fields uses the shared parser, so its refusal carries the whole catalog domain as allowed_values / legal_domain, keeping its curated example (Codex P2, Greptile); the shared fields tool metadata names package row keys and adds a package example (Codex P3); the inflected did-you-mean follows operands with the bootstrap scanner, so pm extensions --json list and --author <value> forms resolve to package list (Codex P3); pm extension list --help now shows the inventory help bundle (CodeRabbit; the cause was a missing extension inventory help entry, not the positional action table)."
  "2026-11-25T08:47:44.771Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 2 listing fixes: the static detector skips root switches and valued root options before the verb (pm package --offline list, --ref v1 list) without reading a value as the verb; bootstrap resolves the package leaf past a scope switch so repeated --fields accumulate (pm package --project list --fields a --fields b); flat MCP/SDK fields now hoist on the root package action, so package-explore/manage/catalog honor a flat fields parameter; pm package list refuses row-shaping read-output controls with read_output_surface_unsupported instead of silently ignoring them (--output-format and --output-budget unbounded still apply); listing --fields refusals carry code invalid_argument_value and recovery.allowed_values with the whole domain for SDK and MCP callers."
  "2026-11-25T09:57:02.996Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 3 listing fixes: one shared lifecycle verb parser (resolveLifecycleVerb in the SDK bootstrap) now serves static selection, bootstrap leaf resolution and plural-noun recovery, so pm --no-changed-fields package list and pm package --offline list stay static (noun found with the host-option grammar), pm package --offline list x --fields=a --fields=b accumulates, and pm extensions --ref v1 list suggests package list. SDK/MCP dispatch of the static listing is recorded as scope on the follow-up listing item."
  "2026-11-25T11:09:27.270Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 4 listing fixes: resolveLifecycleVerb also skips the values of inherited host options (--pm-path, --path, --author, --output-budget and the rest of GLOBAL_VALUE_CONSUMING_FLAGS), so pm package --pm-path /work list stays static and recovery for extensions --author Ada list resolves package list; flat MCP fields hoist on the package and extension actions (HOISTED_ACTION_OPTION_KEYS); pm contracts --command 'package inventory' and 'package list' now return the inventory flags (EXTENSION_INVENTORY_FLAG_CONTRACTS published beside the other lifecycle flag contracts; extension inventory destination and positional rows declared); the harness doc qualifies the refusal to keys with a defined value."
  "2026-11-25T12:13:17.783Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 5 listing fixes: static selection decides on the normalized invocation, so a runner-injected pm token (pm pm package list) and a leading terminator (pm -- package list) stay off extension activation, and an invocation normalization refuses is never static; the legacy extension rewrite also keeps a bare fields= assignment on the subcommand route; pm contracts --command 'extension list' now returns the inventory flags (extension list destination and positional rows declared)."
  "2026-11-25T13:14:56.958Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 6 listing fixes: static selection removes a terminator that follows host options (pm --json -- package list), and pm package list validates the raw --output-format before host option parsing can drop it, refusing an unknown format exactly as other reads do."
  "2026-11-25T14:20:49.199Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 7 listing fixes: the terminator before the command is identified with the host-option grammar (a -- that is the value of --pm-path stays a value), and the legacy extension rewrite matches --fields spellings case-insensitively (--FIELDS, FIELDS=) as normalization does."
  "2026-11-25T15:20:07.131Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 8 listing fix: a refused --fields selection reports only the unknown keys in its message and carries the legal domain in recovery.allowed_values (and refusal.legal_domain in JSON), so human text applies the documented domain bound instead of printing all 22 explore/manage keys."
  "2026-11-25T15:24:18.052Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review round 6: the legacy extension route guard also accepts the fields: shorthand, which the bare-key parser normalizes like fields=, so pm extension explore fields:name keeps its projection."
  "2026-11-25T16:05:44.878Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 9 (Codex: 0 P1, 5 P2, 1 P3). Fixed: pm package list applies the tracker's output.default_format (read from settings.json without the scaffolding settings reader), which the catalog alias honored on main; the terminator before the command is found by walking host options with their arity (removeLeadingCommandTerminator in the SDK bootstrap), so pm --pm-path -- --json -- package list stays static; COMMANDS.md says human text bounds a long field domain and --json carries all of it. Re-reported and already owned: SDK/MCP static listing dispatch (pm-q5iao5) and npm install-resolution provenance (pm-4qq9jy). Not changed, with reason: a FIFO planted at the observation lock path would block core acquireLock metadata reads for every lock in the tracker, not only this one; that is a core lock-primitive concern outside this PR."
  "2026-11-25T18:11:04.184Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 11 listing fixes: the static listing reads the tracker's settings only when no encoding was requested, through the guarded bounded reader, so pm package list --global --output-format json never touches project settings and a non-regular settings file cannot hang it; the deprecated pm extension list spelling keeps its migration hint, read statically from ux.deprecation_hints (on by default)."
  "2026-11-25T20:13:23.083Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 13 listing fixes: installed manifests are read with a bounded, non-blocking read that still follows links (as the runtime loader does), so a FIFO manifest is reported manifest_unreadable instead of hanging pm package list; the static listing refuses lifecycle options of other package actions (--fix-managed-state, --runtime-probe, --trace, --watch, --strict-exit, --fail-on-warn, --isolated, --ignore-global, --detail, --dry-run) instead of silently succeeding, and keeps accepting the already-satisfied --offline."
  "2026-11-25T21:48:27.664Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 14 listing fix: pm package list also refuses the parent command's action selectors and their arguments (--install, --uninstall, --explore, --list, --manage, --describe, --markdown, --output, --reload, --doctor, --catalog, --adopt, --adopt-all, --activate, --deactivate, --migrate, --init, --scaffold, --capability, --declarative, --gh, --github, --ref), which it would otherwise ignore."
  "2026-11-26T04:35:17.893Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 21 on PR #1782 (P3, both fixed): --fields is refused with a usage error on a lifecycle action that shapes no rows (describe, install, doctor and the rest), on the CLI and through MCP and the SDK, instead of being silently ignored; an explore or manage selection is validated before any lifecycle lock is taken, so pm package manage --fix-managed-state --fields typo reports the legal fields instead of a lock or filesystem error."
  "2026-11-26T06:27:32.281Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 23 on PR #1782 (P2, fixed): the legacy-action rewrite kept a pm extension invocation on its subcommand route whenever any argv token looked like a fields projection, including a host flag value (pm --author fields extension install a b took the variadic installer instead of the single-target action route). The bypass now applies only to the explore and manage listings, and only to tokens after the action up to a terminator."
  "2026-11-26T07:35:36.909Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 24 on PR #1782, fixed: the bootstrap lifecycle-leaf scan accepted any operand after root options as the subcommand, so pm package --install ./demo --dry_run took ./demo as the leaf, lost the root flag table and left --dry_run unnormalized (main normalized it); a token found only after root options now counts as the leaf when it names a lifecycle subcommand. The pm package list read-output refusal names the first refused control in its structured flag, never a valid --fields projection. COMMANDS.md says the JSON field domain is complete within the default diagnostic budget and that the SDK error context always holds all of it."
  "2026-11-26T09:20:26.566Z","harness:claude-code","Greptile review round 11 and CodeRabbit review round 15 (fixed): pm package --project upgrade --cli_only again normalizes --cli_only, because the post-option lifecycle leaf check also recognizes upgrade, which has its own flag table outside the lifecycle map; the contract_change migration note now names ExtensionCommandOptions and its optional scope option for consumers that enumerate keys (Record<keyof ...>), and the SDK surface acknowledgement says each change adds an optional member or export that key-enumerating consumers must add, instead of calling it purely additive."
